            "text": "{\"answer\":\"**Total waste generation in France (latest available year 2022)**  \\n\\n| Year | Waste per capita | Approx. population* | Estimated total waste |\\n|------|------------------|---------------------|----------------------|\\n| 2022 | **5 076 kg / inhabitant** | ≈ 67 million people | **≈ 340 million tonnes** |\\n\\n\\\\*Population is the official French estimate for 2022 (≈ 67 million).  \\n\\nThe figure of **5 076 kg per inhabitant** comes from the Eurostat‑based indicator “Total waste generation” which tracks waste from all economic sectors and households[[1]](https://www.eea.europa.eu/en/europe-environment-2025/countries/france/waste-generation). Multiplying this per‑capita value by the national population gives a rough total amount of **~3.4 × 10⁸ t** (≈ 340 Mt) for 2022.\\n\\nThe same Eurostat indicator also expresses waste as an index (2010 = 100 %). In 2022 France’s index value was **92.7 %**, meaning overall waste generation was about 7 % lower than in 2010[[1]](https://www.eea.europa.eu/en/europe-environment-2025/countries/france/waste-generation).  \\n\\n**Take‑away:** France generated roughly **340 million tonnes of waste in 2022**, corresponding to about **5 t per person per year**, which is a modest decline from the 2010 level.\",\"sources\":[\"The indicator shows the total generated amount of all types of waste from all economic sectors and households, and compares it with economic development measured as gross domestic product (GDP).\\nOn track\\nTarget/objective will be reached following the historical trend\\n2010 2015 2020 2025 2030 0 20 40 60 80 100 120\\nHistorical trend France Historical trend EU GDP France GDP EU Total waste generation* Index 2010=100% EU policy objective: significantly reduce total waste generation by 2030\\nDownload\\nShare\\nEnlarge\\nVisualization title: Total waste generation*\\nSecondary label (shown as chart subtitle; may also serve as the y-axis title): Index 2010=100%\\nIn each data section below, every line is one column: its values are listed in row order and align by position across columns  the Nth value in every column belongs to the same record. \\\"-\\\" means no value.\\nData:\\n- EU_gdp_Percent: 100.0, -, 100.839, -, 102.225, -, 106.215, -, 111.048, -, 106.731, -, 116.747, -, -, -, -, -, -, -, -\\n- EU_trend_Total_waste_generation_Percent: 100.0, -, 101.3753238987, -, 100.8969503687, -, 101.1361371337, -, 104.3452262308, -, 96.0135539167, -, 99.4817620092, -, -, -, -, -, -, -, -\\n- France_gdp_Percent: 100.0, -, 101.662, -, 102.446, -, 103.579, -, 106.562, -, 99.901, -, 108.796, -, -, -, -, -, -, -, -\\n- France_trend_Total_waste_generation_Percent: 100.0, -, 96.0934647682, -, 89.3209200438, -, 88.2803943045, -, 93.3187294633, -, 83.5523913837, -, 92.6615553122, -, -, -, -, -, -, -, -\\n\\n- years: 2010, 2011, 2012, 2013, 2014, 2015, 2016, 2017, 2018, 2019, 2020, 2021, 2022, 2023, 2024, 2025, 2026, 2027, 2028, 2029, 2030\\nData Provenance:\\n- data_provenance_link: https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/databrowser/view/env_wasgen__custom_10317000/default/table, https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/databrowser/view/nama_10_pc__custom_10317081/default/table\\n- data_provenance_organisation: Eurostat, Eurostat\\n- data_provenance_title: Generation of waste by waste category, hazardousness and NACE Rev. 2 activity, Gross domestic product (GDP) and main components per capita\\nTemporal Coverage:\\n- temporal_coverage_label: 2010, 2012, 2014, 2016, 2018, 2020, 2022\\nGeographical Coverage:\\n- geo_coverage_label: France\\n*Note: Trends for waste and GDP based on per capita values.\\nAssessment\\nData sources\\nMetadata\\nIn France, waste per capita production fell by 7% between 2010 and 2022, from 5 478 kg per inhabitant per year to 5 076 kg per inhabitant per year. It fell continuously through 2016, then rose up again in 2018 and fell down again in 2020, mainly due to the slowdown in economic activity due to the COVID-19 pandemic. In 2022, waste generation grew again, mainly due to the recovery of construction activity. Municipal waste accounts for around 10% of total waste (535 kg per inhabitant in 2022) .\\nIn order to achieve the global carbon neutrality goal that France has set itself by 2050, Article 3 of Law No 2020-105 of 10 February 2020 on combating waste and the circular economy (the AGEC law) introduces a target of a 5% reduction in the amount of waste from economic activities per unit value produced by 2030 compared with 2010. Over 20102022, GDP per capita was stable. Waste generation thus decreased from 166 kg per thousand euro of value added in 2010 to 138 kg per thousand euro of value added in 2022, a decrease of 17%. The 2030 target is therefore already well achieved.\\nThe EUs policy objective is to significantly reduce total waste production by 2030. \\nIf France continues this trend, this objective should be met.\\n- Generation of waste by waste category, hazardousness and NACE Rev. 2 activity , Eurostat\\n- Gross domestic product (GDP) and main components per capita , Eurostat\\nTopics\\nWaste and recycling\\nBuildings and construction Geographical coverage\\nFrance Temporal coverage\\n2010\\n2012\\n2014\\n2016\\n2018\\n2020\\n2022\\nRelated content\\nReferences and footnotes\\n- CGDD, La production et le recyclage des déchets en 2020 et 2021 en France  Synthèse des connaissances en 2023, CGDD website, 20 November 2023, accessed 16 June 2025, https://www.statistiques.developpement-durable.gouv.fr/la-production-et-le-recyclage-des-dechets-en-2020-et-2021-en-france-synthese-des-connaissances-en?rubrique=395&dossier=1028250 . \\n- CGDD, Bilan 2020 de la production de déchets en France, CGDD website, 25 November 2022, accessed 16 June 2025, https://www.statistiques.developpement-durable.gouv.fr/bilan-2020-de-la-production-de-dechets-en-france?rubrique=&dossier=1028250 . \",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"The indicator shows the total generated amount of all types of waste from all economic sectors and households, and compares it with economic development measured as gross domestic product (GDP).\\nOn track\\nTarget/objective will be reached following the historical trend\\n2010 2015 2020 2025 2030 0 20 40 60 80 100 120\\nHistorical trend France Historical trend EU GDP France GDP EU Total waste generation* Index 2010=100% EU policy objective: significantly reduce total waste generation by 2030\\nDownload\\nShare\\nEnlarge\\nVisualization title: Total waste generation*\\nSecondary label (shown as chart subtitle; may also serve as the y-axis title): Index 2010=100%\\nIn each data section below, every line is one column: its values are listed in row order and align by position across columns  the Nth value in every column belongs to the same record. \\\"-\\\" means no value.\\nData:\\n- EU_gdp_Percent: 100.0, -, 100.839, -, 102.225, -, 106.215, -, 111.048, -, 106.731, -, 116.747, -, -, -, -, -, -, -, -\\n- EU_trend_Total_waste_generation_Percent: 100.0, -, 101.3753238987, -, 100.8969503687, -, 101.1361371337, -, 104.3452262308, -, 96.0135539167, -, 99.4817620092, -, -, -, -, -, -, -, -\\n- France_gdp_Percent: 100.0, -, 101.662, -, 102.446, -, 103.579, -, 106.562, -, 99.901, -, 108.796, -, -, -, -, -, -, -, -\\n- France_trend_Total_waste_generation_Percent: 100.0, -, 96.0934647682, -, 89.3209200438, -, 88.2803943045, -, 93.3187294633, -, 83.5523913837, -, 92.6615553122, -, -, -, -, -, -, -, -\\n\\n- years: 2010, 2011, 2012, 2013, 2014, 2015, 2016, 2017, 2018, 2019, 2020, 2021, 2022, 2023, 2024, 2025, 2026, 2027, 2028, 2029, 2030\\nData Provenance:\\n- data_provenance_link: https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/databrowser/view/env_wasgen__custom_10317000/default/table, https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/databrowser/view/nama_10_pc__custom_10317081/default/table\\n- data_provenance_organisation: Eurostat, Eurostat\\n- data_provenance_title: Generation of waste by waste category, hazardousness and NACE Rev. 2 activity, Gross domestic product (GDP) and main components per capita\\nTemporal Coverage:\\n- temporal_coverage_label: 2010, 2012, 2014, 2016, 2018, 2020, 2022\\nGeographical Coverage:\\n- geo_coverage_label: France\\n*Note: Trends for waste and GDP based on per capita values.\\nAssessment\\nData sources\\nMetadata\\nIn France, waste per capita production fell by 7% between 2010 and 2022, from 5 478 kg per inhabitant per year to 5 076 kg per inhabitant per year. It fell continuously through 2016, then rose up again in 2018 and fell down again in 2020, mainly due to the slowdown in economic activity due to the COVID-19 pandemic. In 2022, waste generation grew again, mainly due to the recovery of construction activity. Municipal waste accounts for around 10% of total waste (535 kg per inhabitant in 2022) .\\nIn order to achieve the global carbon neutrality goal that France has set itself by 2050, Article 3 of Law No 2020-105 of 10 February 2020 on combating waste and the circular economy (the AGEC law) introduces a target of a 5% reduction in the amount of waste from economic activities per unit value produced by 2030 compared with 2010. Over 20102022, GDP per capita was stable. Waste generation thus decreased from 166 kg per thousand euro of value added in 2010 to 138 kg per thousand euro of value added in 2022, a decrease of 17%. The 2030 target is therefore already well achieved.\\nThe EUs policy objective is to significantly reduce total waste production by 2030. \\nIf France continues this trend, this objective should be met.\\n- Generation of waste by waste category, hazardousness and NACE Rev. 2 activity , Eurostat\\n- Gross domestic product (GDP) and main components per capita , Eurostat\\nTopics\\nWaste and recycling\\nBuildings and construction Geographical coverage\\nFrance Temporal coverage\\n2010\\n2012\\n2014\\n2016\\n2018\\n2020\\n2022\\nRelated content\\nReferences and footnotes\\n- CGDD, La production et le recyclage des déchets en 2020 et 2021 en France  Synthèse des connaissances en 2023, CGDD website, 20 November 2023, accessed 16 June 2025, https://www.statistiques.developpement-durable.gouv.fr/la-production-et-le-recyclage-des-dechets-en-2020-et-2021-en-france-synthese-des-connaissances-en?rubrique=395&dossier=1028250 . \\n- CGDD, Bilan 2020 de la production de déchets en France, CGDD website, 25 November 2022, accessed 16 June 2025, https://www.statistiques.developpement-durable.gouv.fr/bilan-2020-de-la-production-de-dechets-en-france?rubrique=&dossier=1028250 . \",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"The indicator shows the total generated amount of all types of waste from all economic sectors and households, and compares it with economic development measured as gross domestic product (GDP).\\nOn track\\nTarget/objective will be reached following the historical trend\\n2010 2015 2020 2025 2030 0 20 40 60 80 100 120\\nHistorical trend France Historical trend EU GDP France GDP EU Total waste generation* Index 2010=100% EU policy objective: significantly reduce total waste generation by 2030\\nDownload\\nShare\\nEnlarge\\nVisualization title: Total waste generation*\\nSecondary label (shown as chart subtitle; may also serve as the y-axis title): Index 2010=100%\\nIn each data section below, every line is one column: its values are listed in row order and align by position across columns  the Nth value in every column belongs to the same record. \\\"-\\\" means no value.\\nData:\\n- EU_gdp_Percent: 100.0, -, 100.839, -, 102.225, -, 106.215, -, 111.048, -, 106.731, -, 116.747, -, -, -, -, -, -, -, -\\n- EU_trend_Total_waste_generation_Percent: 100.0, -, 101.3753238987, -, 100.8969503687, -, 101.1361371337, -, 104.3452262308,